# An ALLOW-LIST: everything is ignored except the few things the image is built from.
#
# This is not a deny-list on purpose. Docker's ignore matching is not .gitignore's: a
# bare `.env` matches only at the root of the build context, where .gitignore's matches
# at any depth. So a deny-list that names `.env`, `CLAUDE.local.md` or `*.pem` keeps
# them out of the root and lets `src/between_jobs/api/.env` straight through into the
# image -- where `load_dotenv()` would then read it at runtime. (Found in review; a
# stray .env with `WORKER_LEASES=off` silently turned the leases off.) Listing what IS
# wanted cannot miss a file nobody thought of. The Dockerfile COPYs exactly these.
*

# hatchling builds the wheel from these; the readme and the license file are metadata
# it reads, so they must stay.
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE

# The package: its Python, its type marker, and the one data file it reads at run time
# (api/geo_gazetteer.py, via importlib.resources). A new data file under the package
# has to be allowed here too -- tests/test_container_static.py fails until it is.
!src/between_jobs/**/*.py
!src/between_jobs/py.typed
!src/between_jobs/api/data/geo_country_aliases.json
**/__pycache__
